   "final": ") | 38,264 orders, 43,513 order lines, 25 listings, 25 ASINs and FNSKUs, 49 FBA shipments |\n| 3PL | 49 items, 29 receipts, 146 receipt lines, 37,331 outbound lines |\n| QuickBooks `vendors.csv` | 11 vendors |\n| Supplier documents | Only the 41 commercial invoice and packing list PDFs, for factory codes and HS codes |\n\n- **Outbound lines:** the 3PL file has no repeated order and item pairs.\n- **Receipt references:** 10 receipts have a blank PO reference, so I wrote no PO ref for them. Rows listing several POs became several refs.\n- **Left out:**\n  - The QuickBooks transaction list is ledger data.\n  - The other supplier PDFs (proformas and inspection reports), the 8 WeChat chats and the ops inbox belong to the ingestion skill.\n\n## Crosswalk\n49 SKU hubs, 1 to 1 across Shopify, the 3PL and the factories. Every hub carries a Shopify variant ID, UPC, 3PL item code, factory item code, HS code and supplier.\n\n| System or link | Tier | Hubs |\n|---|---|---|\n| Shopify variant | exact, confidence 1 | 43 |\n| Shopify variant | normalized, 0.9 | 6 |\n| 3PL item code | exact, matched on UPC | 49 |\n| Factory item code, HS code, supplier | corroborated, 0.7, matched on description | 49 |\n| Amazon listing | exact | 12 |\n| Amazon listing | normalized, 0.9, `-FBA` suffix dropped | 13 |\n\n- **Shopify normalized hubs:** these are the six with malformed Shopify codes, such as `AHUTN0017NAT`, `ah-btl-0020-blk` and `AH-TPT-23-CLR`. I used the corrected pattern spelling as the hub code.\n- **3PL:** five items have a blank Client SKU, and several others are mistyped (`BKL`, `SVL`, `HFL`, `BMA`). UPC resolved all of them.\n- **Amazon listing counts:** I counted listings by comparing seller SKUs with the hub codes in the data. I did not re-query the store to confirm 12 and 13.\n- **Suppliers:** 8 suppliers. QuickBooks names match 8 of the 11 vendors (confidence 0.9). The other 3 (the forwarder, the broker and the 3PL) are indexed under their QuickBooks name only.\n- **Unmatched:** nothing. Every Amazon seller SKU, 3PL item and factory item found a hub.\n\n## Attributes registered\nNone. The installed vocabulary covered every identifier and join key.\n\n## Duplicates marked\n154 `core/same_as` links, each newer account pointing at the oldest.\n- **Plus-alias mailbox (0.9):** 84 links. Ten sampled pairs share the name and address.\n- **Same name and postal address (0.7):** 70 links. Ten sampled pairs share the name and address.\n- **Reading the sample:** some accounts also ship to gift recipients. The account names match in every pair I looked at.\n- **Largest cluster:** no account has more than two others pointing at it.\n\n## Step 7 checks\n- **Bare records:** 26 PO numbers carry only `po/number`. These are the POs the receipts name, and the ingestion skill will fill them. The only other bare records are the 3 vendors above and customers, which hold just their ID.\n- **Duplicates:** the same-account checks above found no wrong pairs.\n- **Counts:** all match the source.\n\n## Terms the sources disagree on\n- **SKU:** the 3PL's \"Client SKU\" is hand-typed (typos or blank). Amazon's seller SKU carries `-FBA` on some listings. Shopify has six malformed spellings. I did not store the 3PL's spelling.\n- **On hand:** the 3PL's On Hand includes damaged units, and Shopify's inventory matches the 3PL's Available (on hand minus allocated). Amazon's total includes unsellable and reserved units. Quantities stay in the sources.\n\n## For you to decide\n- **Receipt to shipment:** the 3PL's container number or house bill of lading names a shipment, but there's no `receipt/shipment` attribute. Container numbers aren't unique identifiers either. I left it for the ingestion step.\n- **Amazon listings:** each seller SKU maps to a different hub, so I found no pair of our codes listed under one ASIN.\n- **Authority:** I recorded field authority for Shopify, Amazon, 3PL and QuickBooks identifiers. I left `sku/code` and `supplier/code` unset, since they are our own codes.\n\n`load.py` is in the working directory.",
