   "final": "I read all three folders into the fact store, and the final state looks consistent.\n\nI made one mistake along the way. My first write run attached shipment lines to the wrong entity. That left 31 duplicate shipment entities, self-referencing `part_of` facts and lines with no shipment. I retracted everything on the duplicates (the history keeps the retractions) and fixed the script. A re-run then rewrote everything correctly, so every shipment now carries both its booking number and its house bill. That re-run replayed the PO ETD values in order, so those attributes' history has extra assert/retract pairs. Final values are right, for example PO-2025-0146 ends at 26 Nov.\n\n**Documents read:**\n\n| Kind | Count |\n|---|---|\n| Proforma invoices | 48 |\n| Commercial invoice / packing lists | 41 |\n| Inspection reports | 46 |\n| WeChat messages | 811 in 8 chats; 124 produced facts |\n| Booking confirmations | 32 |\n| Rolled bookings | 4 |\n| Pre-alerts | 31 |\n| ETA updates | 7 |\n| Arrival notices | 30 |\n| Customs entry summaries | 30 |\n| Warehouse receipts | 29 |\n\nThe 41 commercial invoices were already in the store, cited only for item and HS codes. I read them again for the shipment facts. Nothing was skipped as already read.\n\n**Entities written:** 48 POs with their lines, 32 shipments (31 with a house bill), 166 shipment lines, 46 inspections, 30 customs entries, and details on the 8 suppliers. 431 documents are now in the store.\n\n**Where things ended up:**\n- **POs:** 37 are received, 4 shipped, 1 ready, 5 in production and 1 confirmed.\n- **Shipments:** 29 are delivered, 1 arrived, 1 departed and 1 booked.\n- **Time zones:** I read the chat timestamps as New York time, with daylight saving.\n- **Document dates:** I re-stamped the PDF issue dates as midnight China time, as the skill specifies. The catalogue had written them as midnight UTC.\n\n**Written at confidence below 1 (76 transactions):**\n- **0.8\u20130.9, 43 `po/status` \"in_production\":** from a supplier acknowledging a deposit or saying production had started. The PO comes from the deposit message, or from matching the amount to a PI. Where I could only use the latest PI, it is 0.8.\n- **0.8\u20130.9, 18 `po/etd`:** slips given as month/day with no year, resolved in China time. 0.9 when the message names the PO, 0.85 when it names a PI number.\n- **0.9, 15 `shipment/container_no`:** \"container loaded\" messages that don't name a PO. I took the PO from that supplier's invoice for the same container.\n\n**Not resolved or not recorded:**\n- Every shipment, booking, container, entry and receipt matched. The loosely written PO references in bookings (\"PO144\", \"po 0147\") all resolved.\n- No HS code on an invoice differed from the SKU's.\n- **Gaps in the vocabulary, left in the documents:**\n  - 4 supplier price changes (+3%, +4%, \u22122%, +5%).\n  - 16 holiday closures.\n  - 82 payment messages (deposits, balances).\n  - 23 sample couriers and packaging samples.\n  - 74 warehouse count and damage discrepancies. Examples are 24 pieces short on one Mingjia bowl line and 21 damaged.\n  - Brokerage fees.\n- **Shipment not yet sailed:** PO-2026-0023 is ready, with its booking PBLXMN2609032 still waiting for a pre-alert.\n\nThe scripts are in the scratchpad (`load.py` and `ingest.py`).",
